      "blocks": {
        "block_yQYdLP": {
          "type": "block",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>According to the FDA guidelines, it is prohibited to mention cure, mitigation, or prevention of any medical conditions or diseases in public posts and advertising for Dietary Supplements.</p><p>Such claims may include (but are not limited to):</p><ul><li>bones problems, inflammation, arthritis, pain...</li><li>illness, health issues, viruses, bacteria, pathogens...</li><li>sexual libido, testosterone, erection, sperm...</li><li>anti-aging, longevity, age-related problems...</li><li>skin issues, scars, pimples, wrinkles, elasticity, dryness...</li><li>detox, heavy metals removal, hangover relief...</li><li>wounds, tissue regeneration, burn, healing...</li><li>memory, Alzheimer's, attention, any brain disorders...</li></ul><p>Please check the following publication for more in-depth info: </p><p><a href=\"https://www.fda.gov/food/food-labeling-nutrition/label-claims-conventional-foods-and-dietary-supplements\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Label Claims for Conventional Foods and Dietary Supplements \">https://www.fda.gov/food/food-labeling-nutrition/label-claims-conventional-foods-and-dietary-supplements</a></p><p>Please avoid using the word health in general as well as treat, healing, prevent, mitigate, etc.</p>",
            "image_type": "image",
            "svg": ""
          }
        },
        "block_WmeVGr": {
          "type": "block",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Those rules are not just about words but applied to the meaning of the sentence or article. If a message has an idea of describing the diseases or medical condition it is strictly prohibited. It is also prohibited to mention health-related issues in the connection to the product even if you cited someone else's article or research. It is also prohibited to have comments or feedback from 3rd parties that mention health-related issues as such comments shall be removed from the post or article.</p><p>If your article or sentence comply (using general terms not connected with a disease or condition such as wellness, wellbeing, metabolism, immunity, beauty in some cases are allowed) but still describe the health-related topics always include the FDA disclaimer:</p><p>\"Dietary Supplements are not intended to diagnose, treat, cure or prevent any disease. The statements made with this article (and any accompanying material) have not been evaluated by FDA and not intended to replace the attention or advice of a physician or other qualified health care professional.\"</p><p><em><strong>Failure to comply will result in your account suspension as well as any affiliation with our brand.</strong></em></p>",
            "image_type": "image",
            "svg": ""
          }
        }
      },
